Upstream gap: an OpenAI connection lists every model its provider returns,
unless its model_ids allowlist replaces that list with fixed IDs, which also
hides every model the provider adds later. Hiding a model otherwise takes a
stored model record, so a deployment cannot leave out one family of a
provider's models, such as the ones a Pipe already serves, while still listing
the rest as the provider changes them. Upstream tracks patterns, excludes
included, in the Model IDs filter as an open idea:
https://github.com/open-webui/open-webui/discussions/23711 (open-webui#33080
was closed as its duplicate).

Add exclude_model_ids to a connection's config in OPENAI_API_CONFIGS: a list
of glob patterns such as ["acme/*", "*embedding*"], matched case-sensitively
against the provider's model IDs before prefix_id applies. Each time Open
WebUI lists models, it leaves the matching ones out of that connection's
list, so they cannot be selected or chatted with through it. Other
connections are unaffected. Any other value hides no model, so a mistyped
config can neither hide a connection's whole list nor break model listing.

Removal check: an Open WebUI release whose Model IDs filter accepts exclude
patterns (discussion #23711); move these patterns there.
--- a/open_webui/routers/openai.py
+++ b/open_webui/routers/openai.py
@@ -650,6 +650,26 @@
                 # Catch non-list responses
                 model_list = []

+            exclude_model_ids = api_config.get('exclude_model_ids')
+            # Only a list of strings matches; a string would match by its characters.
+            if isinstance(exclude_model_ids, list) and exclude_model_ids:
+                from fnmatch import fnmatchcase
+
+                # Patterns match the provider's own model IDs, before prefix_id applies.
+                model_list = [
+                    model
+                    for model in model_list
+                    if not any(
+                        isinstance(pattern, str)
+                        and fnmatchcase(str(model.get('id', model.get('name', ''))), pattern)
+                        for pattern in exclude_model_ids
+                    )
+                ]
+                if isinstance(response, list):
+                    response[:] = model_list
+                else:
+                    response['data'] = model_list
+
